#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161706 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162140 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b371f15-7541-5cd9-ac1c-e53fd3b8fc18" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Correlation Coefficient Given Variances and Covariance"}] :question/id #uuid "284f65cd-1288-56ed-80b7-f611b1464835" :question/math-academy-id "e-10372" :question/problem "The variances of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ are $25$ and $36,$ respectively. Given that $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 18,$ find the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] }{\\textrm {SD}[X] \\cdot \\textrm {SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\textrm {SD}[X]$ and $\\textrm {SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{25}=5, \\\\ \\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[Y]}=\\sqrt{36}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[X]} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{5\\cdot 6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161707 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "d132664b-222c-5dd5-a52b-2471d10fcb25" :question/math-academy-id "e-10373" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\textrm {E}[X]=0.4\\qquad\n\\textrm {E}[Y]=0.6, \\qquad\n\\textrm {SD}[X] \\approx 0.4899, \\qquad\n\\textrm {SD}[Y] \\approx 0.4899,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] }{\\textrm {SD}[X] \\cdot \\textrm {SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\textrm {SD}[X]$ and $\\textrm {SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & +1\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =0.1-(0.4)(0.6) \\\\  & =-0.14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.14}{0.4899\\cdot 0.4899} \\\\  & ≈-0.58,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161708 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51a3f265-d2dd-5e62-931e-4bf6d7597ea4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "6562853a-696d-5cb5-a79d-76ff1a084d90" :question/math-academy-id "e-10384" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9cf18d64c3f283c730e1d32ee81e3f193e615bb7b0b936dac009c46328826b3d.svg)\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\textrm {E}[X]= \\dfrac{3}{4},\\qquad\n\\textrm {E}[Y]= \\dfrac{5}{12}, \\qquad\n\\textrm {SD}[X]\\approx 0.1936, \\qquad\n\\textrm {SD}[Y]\\approx 0.2444,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] }{\\textrm {SD}[X] \\cdot \\textrm {SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\textrm {SD}[X]$ and $\\textrm {SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}xy\\cdot 2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}(2{x}^{2}y+2x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-(\\frac{3}{4})(\\frac{5}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(\\frac{1}{48})}{(0.1936)\\cdot (0.2444)} \\\\  & ≈0.44,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162140 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b371f15-7541-5cd9-ac1c-e53fd3b8fc18" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Correlation Coefficient Given Variances and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9badd4d5-fa7a-524f-8a4d-c7d955a67763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159843} {:answer/id #uuid "da1e4ddf-ca69-5ec1-9743-a0a9874f78c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159844} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3f7df6-924d-5b9c-b67b-d3772cb7294b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159845} {:answer/id #uuid "11be860b-a007-55a2-bb06-bac076846dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159846} {:answer/id #uuid "390481e4-d8e5-5074-a53e-1a43032d2ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "390481e4-d8e5-5074-a53e-1a43032d2ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159847} :answer-field/id #uuid "413e7a4f-2d36-5cc3-8768-9d8e9ee9a713" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a81cd707-e6c5-5113-8dea-ede53eaaf544" :question/math-academy-id "q-146468" :question/problem "Given that $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=5,$ $\\text{SD}[X]=2,$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]=4$, find the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6835da4f-0783-54f5-9112-499b793c7b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416492} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3b6071-447a-5e5b-955a-60e039ddb364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416494} {:answer/id #uuid "84a27511-2f73-51ad-9efc-512adfb8573b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416496} {:answer/id #uuid "f032cbc3-7ec5-5ffd-9b44-86c708965b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416501} {:answer/id #uuid "f2544fdb-11f6-5f6b-b648-844f55f4831f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d3b6071-447a-5e5b-955a-60e039ddb364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416494} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd07d7b1-6cdf-5103-98fc-8aa75014e305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86b78d29-f123-58f2-82ad-24e8b4486f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-146471" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.6,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=1,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4899,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.8944,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & +1\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =0.5-(0.6)(1) \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.1}{0.4899\\cdot 0.8944} \\\\  & ≈0.23,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51a3f265-d2dd-5e62-931e-4bf6d7597ea4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "304f73f4-0397-5854-960b-762988f4153d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546356} {:answer/id #uuid "62ec7766-2c11-5907-b71d-e497ceab6d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546467} {:answer/id #uuid "64e5f106-8480-5a83-97f5-e5174d418982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546473} {:answer/id #uuid "b56517bb-ec5e-584d-9307-e3e474bb3360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546657} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb85af9-dc03-5f44-8022-ff6dccdd0429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b56517bb-ec5e-584d-9307-e3e474bb3360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546657} :answer-field/id #uuid "abcaf86c-3cea-5f12-a174-9ce2866296f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2265fb13-ede5-5876-96c9-a4518515ab31" :question/math-academy-id "q-148337" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{9},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{5}{9},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.5329,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2833,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot \\frac{x+y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-(\\frac{11}{9})(\\frac{5}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{81})}{(0.5329)\\cdot (0.2833)} \\\\  & ≈-0.08,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51a3f265-d2dd-5e62-931e-4bf6d7597ea4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dbf269c-de52-5987-8c5f-a5ab6a428860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546276} {:answer/id #uuid "3e34aae8-23b2-5c5e-b6cd-0140500f4a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546390} {:answer/id #uuid "548fd2f9-0377-54ba-80cc-2c84f01bfa2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546434} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c8562d-d0e1-528d-b700-ac3e947458d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.09" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546683} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f73334-b1a2-55a1-9029-06b428581140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8f73334-b1a2-55a1-9029-06b428581140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546807} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2b36089-1198-54b4-93f5-8abdffa58d09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6da1a8e2-af30-5f0e-8a87-d537d126dcee" :question/math-academy-id "q-148358" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)}{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4332,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.4332,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician and integration by parts, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}xy\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[\\frac{\\pi }{2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-y)+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-y)-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-y)]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1)(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1)\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1-(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-4\\pi +8}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-4\\pi +8}{8}-(\\frac{\\pi }{4})(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-8\\pi +16}{16} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-1)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{{(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-1)}^{2}}{(0.4332)\\cdot (0.4332)} \\\\  & ≈0.25,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a338c4-3e34-50f6-a27f-c7bd6f9c731a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546366} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae7ef88-80ec-52bf-b1c6-f25e85e1da32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546418} {:answer/id #uuid "523e5d29-ef3d-533d-b3d9-6739242fa7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546429} {:answer/id #uuid "e23b0d2d-cf61-5bf1-a063-a5a75eae372a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546754} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0bb3cc-ac0e-56cc-9257-49e5bfd7e4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "523e5d29-ef3d-533d-b3d9-6739242fa7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546429} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a7f369-0b11-52c5-910c-d3314793473c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7da918be-db4c-59cf-8e95-bb2e34ce04e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-148366" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ | $0.8$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.8\\,\\text{E}[Y]=0.7,\\,\\text{SD}[X]=0.4,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.4583,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & +1\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.2+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =0.6-(0.8)(0.7) \\\\  & =0.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.04}{0.4\\cdot 0.4583} \\\\  & ≈0.22,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "671ca342-974b-595d-90ce-f2d135a933c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416491} {:answer/id #uuid "76b4ff69-0d3b-5cf8-8bc0-c37eb66140b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416493} {:answer/id #uuid "8305d7f0-359a-5672-84b3-d2451cec6023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416495} {:answer/id #uuid "92d2fd3c-8d02-57f3-80c7-ad19c8e18d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416498} {:answer/id #uuid "990379fa-9ca9-5e21-9b76-b06e960628cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d2fd3c-8d02-57f3-80c7-ad19c8e18d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416498} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7baad12-38b1-5f0c-9519-c9cab1926772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "972ce393-9eba-55fd-8649-cb51968b297d" :question/math-academy-id "q-148368" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ | $0.7$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.3\\,\\text{E}[Y]=0.2,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4583,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.9798,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & +1\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0.2+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =-0.1-(0.3)(0.2) \\\\  & =-0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.16}{0.4583\\cdot 0.9798} \\\\  & ≈-0.36,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cc16f2e-0ce4-50e3-9ce6-2fcd93fe8745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546558} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf2dbe1-47bd-52c4-9356-3277c6c0a4b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546559} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9818d8-a03f-553d-80d1-8feae43d018e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546561} {:answer/id #uuid "dc66e48f-2f69-59da-9829-5e8865ac0ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546738} {:answer/id #uuid "e9323ec5-3d84-5f68-a0df-0a2650658c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d9818d8-a03f-553d-80d1-8feae43d018e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546561} :answer-field/id #uuid "7773313f-b6ec-5d71-babd-97a645cc46df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77a83823-b66d-5cc9-b223-222b52ef5845" :question/math-academy-id "q-148375" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-10$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=10$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.45$ | $0.1$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=2,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=0,\\,\\text{SD}[X]=2,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈9.4868,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-10)\\cdot 0.4+0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.05+0\\cdot 10\\cdot 0.05 \\\\  & +4\\cdot (-10)\\cdot 0.05+4\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.05+4\\cdot 10\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =14-(2)(0) \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{14}{2\\cdot 9.4868} \\\\  & ≈0.74,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0876eb83-57bd-5e84-8477-dc5d60ce323d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416488} {:answer/id #uuid "54445a12-3783-54c9-a829-54a3a211f3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416489} {:answer/id #uuid "59e0c0fc-3c74-57a4-869c-4fa2f31bf145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416490} {:answer/id #uuid "90d7f216-f436-5ba1-90e3-d380e7bb6856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416497} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c6d741-b8ea-5c6d-a797-e6668be9d1b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d7f216-f436-5ba1-90e3-d380e7bb6856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416497} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3019da1-a157-5528-94a6-85caf91d61fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71621138-ed93-53b4-9ace-266f4a0d5dab" :question/math-academy-id "q-148377" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-4$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.16$ | $0.17$ | $0.19$ | $0.52$ |\n| $X=10$ | $0.15$ | $0.17$ | $0.16$ | $0.48$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.31$ | $0.34$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=4.8,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=-0.54,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈4.9960,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈2.4634,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.16+0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.17+0\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.19 \\\\  & +10\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.15+10\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.17+10\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.16 \\\\  & =-2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =-2.8-(4.8)(-0.54) \\\\  & =-0.208.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.208}{4.9960\\cdot 2.4634} \\\\  & ≈-0.02,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162140 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b371f15-7541-5cd9-ac1c-e53fd3b8fc18" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Correlation Coefficient Given Variances and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07213644-e5d0-599f-bcd5-6d81d5dcab3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546263} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1ab8cb-ee3f-5b2f-b295-5630ccd06a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546393} {:answer/id #uuid "529d96e9-557a-56e5-95ed-388cec93d53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546431} {:answer/id #uuid "c07daf66-643f-51c9-b5a6-c8358110cee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546682} {:answer/id #uuid "ef55aff8-a3c5-5745-95b9-1636b990fb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef55aff8-a3c5-5745-95b9-1636b990fb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546790} :answer-field/id #uuid "a47ac2fc-ec4f-54bb-92b9-771843969087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "108257b2-5d47-5fa2-8bfe-f9bdb9653702" :question/math-academy-id "q-148378" :question/problem "Given that $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=-3,$ $\\text{SD}[X]=3,$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]=2$, find the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162140 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b371f15-7541-5cd9-ac1c-e53fd3b8fc18" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Correlation Coefficient Given Variances and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105b4854-df99-5057-8819-5e92ecbdc276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546283} {:answer/id #uuid "7105ce47-e65e-58e7-8416-42579ae9d983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546501} {:answer/id #uuid "7f722018-a718-55b8-9443-c65ca8642453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546535} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb1dff9-6371-5445-8912-de016b27357a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{1\\,000}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546707} {:answer/id #uuid "f23b09ee-e89e-507b-97b3-9134a247f261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105b4854-df99-5057-8819-5e92ecbdc276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546283} :answer-field/id #uuid "a17f6816-6b84-5155-8989-9c88ab516dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ca653e0-5f41-50c6-a86a-21726824fff4" :question/math-academy-id "q-148379" :question/problem "Given that $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=15,$ $\\text{SD}[X]=10,$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]=5$, find the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{10\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162140 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b371f15-7541-5cd9-ac1c-e53fd3b8fc18" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Correlation Coefficient Given Variances and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491e9d0b-9b7f-5df2-8441-12f39280dcca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546416} {:answer/id #uuid "493345f6-3f83-55ac-8af5-48356e149a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546417} {:answer/id #uuid "920b07a2-8356-5fba-b8aa-97c20731338b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546573} {:answer/id #uuid "a2de847a-7013-521b-a7f6-357f040b7f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546615} {:answer/id #uuid "fd63aed9-5fc4-5aa6-a25f-ac276071a085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd63aed9-5fc4-5aa6-a25f-ac276071a085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546821} :answer-field/id #uuid "2212179e-ed1f-5db6-9753-e3dbbfa7a2a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a6faf2d-d933-5235-81aa-8381b3e3dfb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-148382" :question/problem "Given that $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=-9,$ $\\text{SD}[X]=2,$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]=5$, find the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{2\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162140 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b371f15-7541-5cd9-ac1c-e53fd3b8fc18" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Correlation Coefficient Given Variances and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b160291-9a4a-556f-855b-a1bdecb15fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546381} {:answer/id #uuid "435e667b-b76a-52f3-8eb3-88f6a0476ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546402} {:answer/id #uuid "7263a393-17bc-5b22-a37e-7d6c9f7fc792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546503} {:answer/id #uuid "afca3ed1-0cc7-5272-8c37-2c485a548b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546643} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b60ac1-9510-5724-96d4-4f6222565e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afca3ed1-0cc7-5272-8c37-2c485a548b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546643} :answer-field/id #uuid "02c6ffe8-da28-5f04-9f10-7f5fb39f6c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "725ce851-768b-5450-a6f8-19b77ae7d6ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-148383" :question/problem "The variances of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ are $0.09$ and $0.16$, respectively. Given that $\\text{Cov}(X,Y)=-0.03,$ find the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{0.09}=0.3, \\\\ \\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[Y]}=\\sqrt{0.16}=0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[X]} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.03}{0.3\\cdot 0.4} \\\\  & =-0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51a3f265-d2dd-5e62-931e-4bf6d7597ea4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ecfb71-5181-5349-90d0-aa801ee90c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546260} {:answer/id #uuid "15d9b08c-5b84-5d59-a03e-eb48b8bdcf05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546298} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc96e3f-b048-53f6-bbac-fc83895ed411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546311} {:answer/id #uuid "318edee1-713f-5f01-ae45-ef3fc7f1957c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546358} {:answer/id #uuid "75eeae67-abff-51e8-b38b-9678a6cab699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "318edee1-713f-5f01-ae45-ef3fc7f1957c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546358} :answer-field/id #uuid "f36d3cec-3da7-547e-beb8-441c3e66c73b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37a89027-b700-5936-918f-1cda621eae37" :question/math-academy-id "q-148419" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{7}{12},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.2898,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2764,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot (\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{x}+\\frac{1}{2}xy)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{2}{3x}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{2}{3x}+\\frac{1}{4}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}+\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}+\\frac{3}{8})-(\\frac{3}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)(\\frac{7}{12}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}-\\frac{7\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{12})+(\\frac{3}{8}-\\frac{7}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{12}-\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{12}-\\frac{1}{16})}{(0.2898)\\cdot (0.2764)} \\\\  & ≈-0.06,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51a3f265-d2dd-5e62-931e-4bf6d7597ea4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1110af6f-ee8e-5716-bb31-7201313d5605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546285} {:answer/id #uuid "69f2cc06-4c6a-5ecd-8241-6b6fdbb489e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546483} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca9fba2-d820-5756-9477-e3b30e8c81f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.03" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546492} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff3df5c-e073-5d90-a4a7-c734d4432894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546564} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f2e5b8-6c24-59e1-81ab-09386b360221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1110af6f-ee8e-5716-bb31-7201313d5605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546285} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aa03162-aa27-5b75-80f4-0a2a94c5c65e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "86de9def-10fe-5788-a466-3607900726ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-148421" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{12}(xy+1), & \\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{1}{7},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.2619,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.4238,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}xy\\cdot \\frac{9}{12}(xy+1)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y]}_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{8}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}{[\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{27}{y}^{9}-\\frac{1}{12}{y}^{6}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}[\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{27}-\\frac{1}{12}-(-\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{27}-\\frac{1}{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}(\\frac{2}{9}-\\frac{2}{27}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}-(\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{315}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(\\frac{8}{315})}{(0.2619)\\cdot (0.4238)} \\\\  & ≈0.23,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51a3f265-d2dd-5e62-931e-4bf6d7597ea4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116e1223-c9c0-50e1-9796-7612d14b69d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546288} {:answer/id #uuid "3af52246-e75a-5df3-a2e8-127297df4308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546380} {:answer/id #uuid "cee2766c-0382-569e-bb67-a703ad240c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546712} {:answer/id #uuid "e3bf9b68-0dfc-54cc-a6bb-ef6cd1976695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546759} {:answer/id #uuid "fc396241-6675-55dc-9a31-e2e02c8f817b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "116e1223-c9c0-50e1-9796-7612d14b69d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546288} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e55990-2ad1-513e-bcc2-f70980e885ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db6e411e-8a97-527f-83cb-17311240c8a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-148422" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{\\pi }, & \\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{8}{5\\pi },\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{8}{5\\pi },\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.2719,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2719,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}xy\\cdot \\frac{8({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }\\text{ }{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}({x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}y+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{1}{4}{(1-{y}^{2})}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}(1-{y}^{2}){y}^{3}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}[(1-2{y}^{2}+{y}^{4})y+2(1-{y}^{2}){y}^{3}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }-(\\frac{8}{5\\pi })(\\frac{8}{5\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{50\\pi -192}{75{\\pi }^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(\\frac{50\\pi -192}{75{\\pi }^{2}})}{(0.2719)\\cdot (0.2719)} \\\\  & ≈-0.64,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}]}
